NNAAMMEE
     uummaassss — USB Mass Storage Devices driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following line in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee ssccbbuuss
           ddeevviiccee uussbb
           ddeevviiccee uummaassss

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           umass_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The uummaassss driver provides support for Mass Storage devices that attach to
     the USB port.

     To use the uummaassss driver, usb(4) and one of uhci(4) or ohci(4) or ehci(4)
     or xhci(4) must be configured in the kernel.  Additionally, since uummaassss
     uses the SCSI subsystem and sometimes acts as a SCSI device, it requires
     da(4) and scbus(4) to be included in the kernel.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
           device umass
           device scbus
           device da
           device pass

     Add the uummaassss driver to the kernel.

           camcontrol rescan 0:0:0
           camcontrol rescan 0:0:1
           camcontrol rescan 0:0:2
           camcontrol rescan 0:0:3

     Rescan all slots on a multi-slot flash reader, where the slots map to
     separate LUNs on a single SCSI ID.  Typically only the first slot will be
     enabled at boot time.  This assumes that the flash reader is the first
     SCSI bus in the system and has 4 slots.

